---
/**
 * t40 · Gloss
 *
 * The same universal oval, read as blown glass.
 *
 * Every other mark in this set keeps its middle calm by deciding to. This one
 * keeps it calm because of what it is made of. A curved gloss reflects least
 * where it faces you and most at a glancing angle, so the Fresnel term alone
 * puts the entire tone spend in the outer band: the turn, the specular
 * crescent and the bounce all gather at the rim, and the crown comes out
 * plain without being told to.
 *
 * The highlight is placed by the light, not by hand. It lands on the upper
 * left shoulder because that is where the surface normal bisects the light
 * and the eye — which is also, usefully, clear of the face. Opposite it the
 * far rim picks up bounce, the small lift that tells you a body is round
 * rather than merely dark on one side.
 *
 * Past the body the ellipsoid has no normal left to give, so the tail is lit
 * off the silhouette itself, from the same direction. It keeps a lit left
 * flank and a shaded right one, and stays a continuation of the oval rather
 * than a shape borrowed from somewhere else.
 *
 * Eleven violets, in a ramp cut so its dark half clears 4.5:1 against the
 * white face and its light half is spent only where the face cannot reach.
 * The middle measures 5.18:1.
 */
import MarkFrame from '../MarkFrame.astro';
import { facePathsAt } from '../../../data/mark';

interface Props { size?: number }
const { size = 128 } = Astro.props;
---

<MarkFrame size={size} title="Strozz — Gloss">
